# Windows agent shell (this machine)

Cursor on native Windows cannot enforce `workspace_readwrite`. The helper is a network proxy only. A default Shell is refused with “sandbox policy unsupported” and **never starts**.

This repo is Windows-native (WPF, kpacket2/MSVC/Ashita). Do not switch the agent to Remote-WSL to get Landlock.

## Do

- Treat a sandbox-policy failure as “needs unsandboxed approval,” not as a hard stop.
- Re-run the same Shell with `required_permissions: ["all"]` and wait for the user to approve.
- Keep using in-workspace Write/StrReplace and GitHub MCP without Shell.

## Do not

- Retry the sandboxed Shell in a loop.
- Enable Run Everything or Legacy Terminal to fake a sandbox.
- Abort the task because the sandbox backend is missing.
